 ## Example response
 
 The settings GET returns a safe configuration view without the full secret. Booking tools return structured outcomes such as created, rescheduled, cancelled, needs_info or an error; use the actual result rather than a fixed success sentence.
+
+## Set and verify a number’s booking zone
+
+Send a [number update](/api-reference/phone-numbers/update) with `{"calcom_timezone_override":"America/New_York"}`. Send JSON `null` to inherit again. Omit the field to preserve it. Use an IANA zone so future appointments follow the branch’s local clock changes. Numeric offsets and empty strings are invalid. Send moves and credential changes as separate requests.
+
+Read the [number](/api-reference/phone-numbers/get) or its [Cal.com status](/api-reference/integration-settings/get-integrations-calcom-number-phoneNumber). The first available value wins: number, agent, saved connection, then `Europe/London`. The effective value and its source appear only with a booking context. You can save a number preference before booking is available. A saved connection on an unassigned number can still report `booking_available: false`.
+
+On inbound and outbound phone calls, a changed target for rescheduling or cancellation needs a complete spoken read-back and a later yes. A fresh lookup, an interrupted read-back or approval of a previous appointment cannot authorise the changed target. During clock changes, ask for another local time if the requested minute is skipped or ambiguous.
 
