+## When an existing Cal.com appointment changes
+
+During either direction of a phone call, the agent may look up the caller’s appointments more than once. If the selected appointment changes, disappears and returns, or the calendar changes, the agent must read the selected appointment’s current details aloud and finish speaking before accepting a new yes to cancel or reschedule it. This protection also applies when optional booking confirmation is off. An unaffected appointment keeps its usual checks. SMS follows its separate approval flow.
+
+For example, if a 10:00 appointment now appears at 11:00, a yes to 10:00 does not approve moving 11:00. Check the calendar result after the caller confirms.
+
